<title>USA: U.S. Cattle on Feed - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. Cattle on Feed - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA U.S. cattle on feed. 7 states, 1,000-plus head feedlots (data in 1,000 head):</p>
<p>    -			Pct----1997----1996    1995</p>
<p> On Feed January 1     103   8,943   8,667   8,031</p>
<p> During December:	Pct----1996----1995    1994</p>
<p> -Placed on Feed	  98   1,423   1,446   1,345</p>
<p> -Marketed		 100   1,415   1,412   1,432</p>
<p> -Other Disappearance  131	68	52	80</p>
<p> On Feed December 1    104   9,003   8,685   8,198</p>
<p>Note--On feed data include cattle placed on feed after beginning of quarter and marketed before the end of quarter.  </p>
<p>USDA cattle on feed in the United States (1,000-plus head feedlots, data in 1,000 head):</p>
<p>    -			Pct----1997----1996</p>
<p> On Feed January 1     102  10,558  10,346</p>
<p> During December:	Pct----1996----1995</p>
<p> -Placed on Feed	  98   1,695   1,728</p>
<p> -Marketed		 101   1,684   1,661</p>
<p> -Other Disappearance  126	86	68</p>
<p> On Feed December 1    103  10,633  10,347</p>
<p>Note--On feed data include cattle placed on feed after beginning of quarter and marketed before the end of quarter.  </p>
<p>Analysts on average had expected the number of cattle on feed in the seven key states on January 1 at 104.2 percent of a year ago, and December placements at 108.2 percent of a year ago. The seven major states are Arizona, California, Colorado, Iowa, Kansas, Nebraska and Texas.</p>
